From: GTS9 Fedora <gts9wifi@local>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: advertise only ARGB8888 output format

DebayerEGL and DebayerCpu advertise four 32-bit RGB variants (XRGB8888,
ARGB8888, XBGR8888, ABGR8888), quadrupling PipeWire/OBS camera format
lists. On GTS9 Fedora, OBS renders XBGR8888 as black and XRGB8888 as
corrupted, while ARGB8888 (PipeWire BGRA) works reliably across OBS,
GNOME Snapshot, Wayland, and browsers.

Restrict advertised SoftwareISP output formats to ARGB8888 only.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -55,10 +55,7 @@
 	BayerFormat bayerFormat =
 		BayerFormat::fromPixelFormat(inputFormat);
 
-	std::vector<PixelFormat> outputFormats = { formats::XRGB8888,
-						   formats::ARGB8888,
-						   formats::XBGR8888,
-						   formats::ABGR8888 };
+	std::vector<PixelFormat> outputFormats = { formats::ARGB8888 };
 
 	if ((bayerFormat.bitDepth == 8 || bayerFormat.bitDepth == 10) &&
 	    bayerFormat.packing == BayerFormat::Packing::None &&
diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp
@@ -432,12 +432,7 @@
 {
 	BayerFormat bayerFormat =
 		BayerFormat::fromPixelFormat(inputFormat);
-	std::vector<PixelFormat> outputFormats = { formats::RGB888,
-						   formats::XRGB8888,
-						   formats::ARGB8888,
-						   formats::BGR888,
-						   formats::XBGR8888,
-						   formats::ABGR8888 };
+	std::vector<PixelFormat> outputFormats = { formats::ARGB8888 };
 
 	if ((bayerFormat.bitDepth == 8 || bayerFormat.bitDepth == 10 || bayerFormat.bitDepth == 12) &&
 	    bayerFormat.packing == BayerFormat::Packing::None &&
